#. Tag: title
#: desktop.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "The desktop"
msgstr "O escritorio"

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I add an application to the desktop?"
msgstr "Como engado un programa ao escritorio?"

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just choose the desired application from the <guimenu>K</guimenu> menu and "
"drag and drop it to the Desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For applications not listed in the <guimenu>K</guimenu> menu, use the &RMB; "
"on the desktop and choose <menuchoice><guimenuitem>Create New</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Link to Application...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and fill in "
"the configuration for the application you want to link to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I mount/unmount a device from the desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, make sure you are allowed to <command>mount</command>/"
"<command>umount</command> the relevant device as a user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then you can add any device by clicking on the desktop with the &RMB; and "
"then choosing <menuchoice><guimenu>Create New</guimenu><guisubmenu>Link to "
"Device</guisubmenu></menuchoice>. Select the device of the type you wish to "
"control. Fill in the settings for the device in the dialog that appears and "
"click <guilabel>OK</guilabel>. You can use the resulting desktop icon to "
"mount/unmount the device from the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where are the icons kept?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The icons can be found only in <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIRS</envar>/share/icons</filename> or <filename class=\"directory"
"\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/icons</filename>. To use icons stored in "
"other locations, you must either copy them into one of the above-mentioned "
"fixed &kde; locations or make symlinks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I use the mouse scroll wheel in &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mouse wheel support comes with &Qt; 2.0 and above, so &kde; based on that "
"will automatically support the use of the mouse scroll wheel if your system "
"is configured correctly. Check that your &X-Server; settings support the use "
"of a scrollwheel if it is not working."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I launch applications in a particular desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; comes with a program called &kstart;. To start an <application>xterm</"
"application> on the second desktop and then activate it use: "
"<userinput><command>kstart</command> <option>--desktop 2 --activate --window "
"\"xterm\" </option>xterm</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that the <option>--window</option> option is important. It takes an "
"argument which is a regular expression matching the title of the window to "
"apply the settings to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please read <command>kstart</command> <option>--help-all</option> for more "
"magic available with &kstart; (and there is an abundance)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Where do I save my files if I want them to appear directly on the desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/Desktop</filename>. You "
"might need to refresh your desktop after you have saved your files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "I've deleted the Trash icon on my desktop. How can I get it back?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: desktop.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Right-click on the desktop and in the context menu that appears, choose "
"<menuchoice><guisubmenu>Create New...</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Link to "
"Location (URL)...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. Set the <guilabel>File name</"
"guilabel> to <userinput>Trash</userinput> and the location to "
"<userinput>trash:/</userinput>. Click on <guibutton>OK</guibutton> and "
"you're done."
msgstr ""
